{"title":"Beautiful Bacteria","link":"https://kottke.org/26/11/beautiful-bacteria","date":1795020240000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980187-a373ccbe.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980187-a373ccbe.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980187-a373ccbe.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980198-e256ac51.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980198-e256ac51.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980198-e256ac51.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980214-0347de45.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980214-0347de45.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980214-0347de45.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980206-e836fba1.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980206-e836fba1.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980206-e836fba1.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980222-12263ff5.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980222-12263ff5.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794980222-12263ff5.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>Tal Danino is a synthetic biologist who works with bacteria, scientifically and artistically.  His aesthetic explorations of bacteria, <a href=\"https://www.taldaninoart.com/bacteria-gallery-1\">Microbial Rainbow</a> and <a href=\"https://www.taldaninoart.com/microuniverse\">Microuniverse</a>, have resulting in a book called <a href=\"https://bookshop.org/a/2966/9780847899869\">Beautiful Bacteria</a> (<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0847899861/ref=nosim/0sil8\">Amazon</a>). You can check out more of his bacterial photos at <a href=\"https://ideas.ted.com/gallery-the-most-beautiful-bacteria-youll-ever-see\">TED</a>, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/gallery/2024/may/18/beautiful-bacteria-encounters-in-the-microuniverse-tal-danino\">The Guardian</a>, <a href=\"https://seed.com/cultured/7-mind-blowing-images-of-microbes\">Seed</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2024/10/29/beautiful-bacteria\">The Marginalian</a>.\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/bacteria\">bacteria</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Tal%20Danino\">Tal Danino</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"a0abdc98297fdfcb4e0a39f93e9a2cba7b80d05f6fed20b3f10adbe4fe5266de","category":"Sites"}